<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koy-Krylgan-Kala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Koy-Krylgan-Kala is an ancient circular monument in Karakalpakstan, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, built in the 4th century BCE in the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>. Its round central building, surrounded by a fortified ring, is thought to have served as a temple, a royal tomb and an astronomical observatory, and it was used until about the 4th century CE. It was excavated by Sergei Tolstov's Khorezm expedition from 1952.</p></div>
